  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 111 AM CST Mon Nov 16 2026\n\nWith high pressure overhead currently and calm winds at the\nsurface and light winds aloft, fog has developed across parts \nof northwest IN and is possible across most of the area outside \nof Chicago this morning. Fog with visibilities below one mile \nwill be possible across northwest IN and will need to monitor \ntrends with some locally dense fog possible. Low level winds are\nexpected to remain strong enough tonight into early Tuesday \nmorning to prevent fog development for most of the area. Should \nany patchy/shallow fog develop, it would be favored across the \nsoutheast cwa.\n\nHigh temps have been above guidance for the past few days and\nthis trend is likely to continue this week with high temps in\nthe 50s through Wednesday (possibly tagging 60 Wednesday) and\nthen high temps are expected to be in the lower/mid 60s Thursday\nthrough Saturday, above normal every day this week.\n\nA storm system is expected to move across the northern Plains\nWednesday and into Ontario Thursday, well north of the local\narea. Models had previously shown a chance of showers with a\nweak trailing cold front on Thursday but are now mainly dry with\nthe front dissipating and then winds turning south/southeast\nFriday as a stronger system develops over the Plains and lifts\nnorth into Ontario Saturday night. A stronger trailing cold\nfront from this system is expected to move across the local area\nSaturday afternoon/night bringing a chance of showers and much\ncooler temps, though only back to near normal. cms",
